# Setup-mode (group assignment) captures, 2026-11-12
#
# Working remote. Its ID is redacted as yy yy / yyyy. Shade: one already in
# group 4 for this remote, so OPEN only re-added an existing entry.
# Receiver: one nRF24 clone module at the `hd` preset (ch 33, 2 Mbps, E7E7E7,
# CRC-16, 5-byte payload), filter off (one line per run of identical packets).
# IR: VS1838B/TSOP on GPIO 14, `ir` capture, remote a few inches from it.
# Lines are copied from the serial monitor; timestamps are the PC's.

## 1. RF: setup + group 4 + OPEN (add), aimed at the shade, which jogged
#
# The first attempt timed out (too slow to reach the shade). The remote left
# setup mode, so that OPEN was a normal red-mode press: the four mode-01 runs
# below, and the shade moved up, then stopped on the next press. Second
# attempt: SETUP, 4, OPEN (the mode-30 run; the shade jogged), then SETUP to
# save. SETUP and the group key sent nothing on ch 33, nor did the save press.

08:05:32.344 > Sniffing. One line per run of identical packets. Send any line to stop.
